\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden: It May Look Bad, But It Is Not A Recession; Job Growth Last Quarter Was Overstated By One Million; Our Government Isn't Telling The Full Truth About UFOs; Wisconsin UFO Eyewitness Talks To Tucker; Man Who Exposed Penis To Girls In Locker Room Has Been Arrested After 15 Months At Large; Detransitioner Is Suing Medical Team That Allowed Her To Cut Off Her Breast; Semafor's Ben Smith Won't Give Back His Scammer Dollars; Stanford Publishes Index Of Forbidden Words; US Antibiotic Shortage Is About To Get Worse; Video Shows Chinese People Lining Up At A Pharma Factory To Get Painkillers As Lockdowns End; Interview With Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R-MO)\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Vivek Ramaswamy, Trace Gallagher, Marc Siegel \par \uc2 8,103 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I have a feeling there won't be a lot of wrestling.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. DVR "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME."\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is up next.\par \par \uc2 And always remember layer and I'm Watters, and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 This past summer, with just a few months to go before the Midterm Elections, the Biden administration faced a huge problem called the economy. Most voters vote on the basis of the economy and how they feel they're doing and how they feel their country is doing, and their country at the time was not doing well.\par \par \uc2 The US economy had just recorded two consecutive quarters of declining GDP. That's not just an academic observation, that's a technical definition of a recession. Two quarters declining GDP, recession. We're not making that up. You'll find it in every economics textbook ever written. Go look up the one you used in college.\par \par \uc2 But the Biden administration could not admit that. If they admitted that the US was in a recession, they would lose the Senate. They would lose control of both chambers of the Congress. So they had to lie about it.\par \par \uc2 But how do you lie about something that's so easily defined, that everyone can see? Well, you just change the definition. And that's what they did. They came up with a new definition of recession. So, don't look at GDP. That's the old way, the racist way of assessing the economy. Look at holistic factors said the White House. Look at the labor market, for example. The labor market.\par \par \uc2 Well, then, in June, the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  gave them ammunition for their case. The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  issued a report that showed the labor market was strong. They determined that the US economy had added more than a million jobs in the second quarter of this year, from March to June. A million jobs. That's a big deal. It's a big story. And of course, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wasted no time in touting it. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Our job market remains historically strong. Our economy created more than nine million jobs since I came to office, in no small part because of the people on this stage.\par \par \uc2 Our economy created more than one million jobs in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: A million new jobs in the second quarter despite negative growth. Wait a second. How do you get a million new jobs with negative growth? That seems like magic. How is that possible?\par \par \uc2 But no one in the media asked questions. Instead, they repeated the White House line, which was the \uc2 BLS\uc2  report -- the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  report -- showing a million new jobs proves we can't be in a recession. They all said it, "The Jobs Report suggests the Biden economy is not in a recession," wrote "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ." And then, of course, there were other stories like that, too.\par \par \uc2 So on the basis of that and other factors, they won. They now have control of the Senate. And now we get to learn the truth. A million new jobs, really?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Philadelphia Fed\uc2  decided to check those numbers and they found the US economy did not add more than a million jobs in the second quarter of this year. Instead, the net additional jobs was about 10,000. So, that's less than one percent of the job growth the administration claimed.\par \par \uc2 That's not a rounding error. That's not a minor math mistake. This is a country that supposedly sent a man to the moon. We can do math, right?\par \par \uc2 This isn't like thinking you had a hundred bucks in your pocket and finding out you had 85. This is like claiming you had a million dollars in your pocket and finding out you had $10,000.00. This is like claiming you were rich when you were actually bankrupt. This is a lie.\par \par \uc2 So how'd they get it wrong by more than a million jobs? How did they construct this lie? Well, as of tonight, we're not really sure. We now know the \uc2 BLS\uc2  numbers didn't just help \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , though. There was another purpose.\par \par \uc2 These fake numbers also gave the Chairman of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , a justification to continue raising interest rates. On the basis of that report, they can raise rates. Here was Powell just a few days ago.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEROME POWELL\uc2 , US FEDERAL RESERVE CHAIRMAN: Today, the FOMC raised our policy interest rate by a half percentage point. We continue to anticipate that ongoing increases will be appropriate in order to attain a stance of monetary policy that is sufficiently restrictive, to return inflation to two percent over time.\par \par \uc2 Despite the slowdown in growth, the labor market remains extremely tight, with the unemployment rate near a 50-year low. Job vacancy is still very high and wage growth elevated. Job gains have been robust.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Ooh. Every word of that a lie. The justification is a lie. And in fact, as Powell well knows, there are seven million American men of working age who are not working, they are watching the Internet all day.\par \par \uc2 So why are they lying to us about this? Well, the effects are very obvious. Go try and take out a car loan or a home loan or any kind of loan. Or if you have a loan, it's got an adjustable rate, watch how much more you're paying per month. So why are they doing this? Well, the administration wants Powell to raise rates because they think it'll offset the inflation that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policies have caused.\par \par \uc2 But this is a huge problem for everyone else. Raising rates when the economy is faltering and people don't have jobs. If you keep doing that, you could cause an actual collapse.\par \par \uc2 That seems like the course they put us on. The Biden administration got the interest rate hike it wanted even when the labor market has been flatlining.\par \par \uc2 William Beach runs the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2  runs the Department of Labor. They need to explain why anyone should ever trust the most basic economic numbers the government issues ever again. And it's one thing to get the numbers wrong, you know are wrong, what is that? That's what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  should probably answer that question fairly soon. He won't join us tonight either.\par \par \uc2 But Vivek Ramaswamy will. He is an entrepreneur, author of "Nation of Victims," a frequent guest in the show. We're happy to have him tonight.\par \par \uc2 Vivek, thank you so much for coming on. So oops, we got it wrong by a million jobs. This seems like a huge story. I think it's being ignored by pretty much everybody. What do you think we're looking at here?\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: I think it is the governmental equivalent of \uc2 Enron\uc2  cooking the books. At the end of the day, if you lie about these numbers, what other numbers is the government actually going to lie about?\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's right. Exactly.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: They tried to change -- exactly -- and as you pointed out, Tucker, they tried to change the definition of what counts as a recession, well, why not just do the end around and just change the numbers themselves. And I'm going to make a prediction, I think we're going to see more of this behavior going forward. We are going to see more of it, because we're in a double whammy of rising interest rates against the backdrop of disastrous economic policies. That is a formula for economic calamity.\par \par \uc2 But the way you cover it up is push it -- kick the can down the road for as long as you can until the house of cards comes falling down. I think that's what why we are going to see even more of this behavior going forward.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I wish that we could bring more facts to the story and in the short time that we had today, we couldn't. But I'm just amazed that you could doctor a foundational economic number like that, like the Jobs Report, that's not some esoteric thing. That's a basic thing upon which people make all kinds of decisions. How do you fake that by a million jobs?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: That's right, and I don't even think, Tucker, this is necessarily \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , even knowing that was the number.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Right.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Of course, the people we elect to run the government, as you well know, are not the people running the government.\par \par \uc2 This is the oldest bureaucratic trick in the playbook. You get to make the rules if I get to fill in the numbers. The people who fill in the numbers hold the keys to the kingdom. That is what the bureaucratic managerial class in government recognizes, put it on the teleprompter, give them right numbers to read out. But the people who tilt the scales of that math are ultimately actually tilting the scales of the public policymakers who are really just the puppets who dance to the tunes to the people who actually report the numbers. That's what's going on here.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Really quick, I just -- I can't resist asking since you're in the business world, you've got a lot of your own money at stake. You know a lot of other people who are in the same position.\par \par \uc2 When you make decisions. Do you look at \uc2 BLS\uc2  numbers? Like, is this part of your calculation as a businessman?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: This is one input that matters, Tucker, but it is part of a broader set of variables that the question is when you undermine trust in the entire reporting mechanism of this particular figure, I think it undermines trust in all of the other figures you get to.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's right.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes, these jobs numbers on a quarterly basis matter. But this is bigger than this particular number. It's about integrity in the reporting system itself.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, and I've got some vaccines I'd like to sell you. We can talk about it off air. But in the meantime, Vivek, great to see you tonight. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Good to see you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So you just heard Vivek say it, if the government is willing to lie to you about foundational economic data, how many new jobs have we created? If they will do that, then what else are they lying about? Or what are they not lying about?\par \par \uc2 Well, here is one thing they have lied about for decades, like more than 70 years, the truth about those lights you see in the sky. They've just started to tell a small part of the truth. The Pentagon was forced to acknowledge that UFOs are in fact real, you're not crazy for knowing that, but they still can't explain them or discuss what these might be.\par \par \uc2 Now, we did a FOX Nation documentary called "The UFO Files." We spoke to a retired Navy pilot who gave his assessment of what these objects are capable of.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHAD UNDERWOOD, NAVY PILOT WHO FILMED THE 'TIC TAC' UFO VIDEO: We got the footage that you see on the Tic-Tac video, which is it's about 40 to -- 40 secon