ained for protesting COVID lockdowns?\par \par \uc2 Do you regret restricting AirDrop access that protesters used to evade surveillance from the Chinese government? Do you think it's problematic to do business with the communist Chinese Party when they suppress human rights?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: I know they have invested a lot there. It's a big market for them. But is there any -- should there be any accountability?\par \par \uc2 ISSA: There should be accountability.\par \par \uc2 I support -- first of all, I oppose and will speak loudly against China's activities and the growth of its crackdowns. I support sanctions, sanctions that would affect companies, including \uc2 Apple\uc2 , both to hurt the Chinese for what they're doing...\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Right.\par \par \uc2 ISSA: ... and to help companies make a decision to bring things back to the U.S. and other free countries.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Representative Issa, Just moments ago, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  tweeting he's going to release what he's calling the Hunter Biden story suppression that went on at \uc2 Twitter\uc2  at 5:00 p.m. Eastern.\par \par \uc2 What do you expect to see?\par \par \uc2 ISSA: We expect to see a lot of what we have already uncovered, but we expect to see some of the inside stories of who in the administration was talking to people and working with people inside \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We also think we're going to see some interaction between \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and other social media companies. The most important thing is that the new chairman has made it clear this isn't going to happen again. And, even today, he was sanctioned or spoken poorly by President Macron for the fact that he is supporting \uc2 Twitter\uc2  being a free speech platform, rather than tipping the scales in favor of who you like and who you disagree with.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Yes, ironically, you had -- back in November, on November 2, you said: I have seen enough. Ban TikTok.\p