rotests in China have been.\par \par \uc2 JIANLI YANG, FOUNDER/PRESIDENT, CITIZEN POWER INITIATIVES FOR CHINA: Hi. Thank you, Martha. As someone who participates in the Tiananmen protests in 1989, I cannot help fading the ankles of that moment in the events taking place in China. So I think the current demonstrations are very, very significant because they are their first nationwide expressions of this content that the political demands. China has seen since the Tiananmen protests in 1989.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: There were many people killed, massacred after those protests. What do you think is happening in China now because what we're being told is that they are curving some of these very stringent lockdown policies.\par \par \uc2 YANG: Yes. We have seen their first direct result of these demonstrations. Chinese government has agreed to lift some restrictions, the so called zero COVID policies, which was the very reason for people to take to the streets and protest. But I want to remind the world that we cannot underestimate the determination of a \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  and the CCP regime to restore fear. So they need a fear to control.\par \par \uc2 And these demonstrations, these protests have reduced the fear the people have over CCP and the regime. So \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  will do everything in his power to reignite fear while loosening some restrictions, the lockdowns for responding to the pandemic. I think you met well remember a scene in the movie the "Schindler's List," where imprisoned Jewish and engineer was bold enough to make suggestions, which is rife suggestions to the German officer, and a German so reacted by shooting him on the spot but ordered that his suggestions be followed. That is exactly what \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  is doing.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: We're looking at a picture of a man who is having his head held against the street and a hand over his mouth. And I think that photo says a lot. Jianli, thank you very much, Jianli Yang. I hope we'll