that World Cup game, where U.S. just pulled off victory against Iran.\par \par \uc2 That game happening in the middle of rising tensions, obviously, Congressman, I just wanted to get your thoughts on that and the political hostility that we have seen around those games.\par \par \uc2 MCCAUL: Well, you know what is great, Sandra, is, the United States just beat Iran today 1-0 in the World Cup. That is fantastic news.\par \par \uc2 And it just shows you once again, whether it's China, Russia, North Korea or Iran, this sort of censoring free speech -- they got mad at their own players who didn't sing the Iranian national anthem, or the U.S. player that had the Iranian flag without the Islamic Republic symbol on it.\par \par \uc2 China does this as well. They censor people, surveil, Russia, North Korea, Iran. They're all axis of evil. They're all aligned with each other. And we need to stand up for the people of Iran as well and the women of Iran who've been so brutally cracked down upon by the ayatollah and the IRGC. We have to have their back as well.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: And now the USA will advance to play the Netherlands in the World Cup knockout round.\par \par \uc2 But thank you very much, Congressman, for joining us on all of that. We appreciate your time today, sir. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MCCAUL: Thank you, Sandra.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: And, as I just mentioned, the U.S. men's national soccer team, here is the celebration, beating Iran 1-0 in the World Cup, advancing to the knockout stage.\par \par \uc2 This is a brand-new video of the fans here at home in the United States celebrating that big win.\par \par \uc2 Let's get right to Alex Hogan. She is in Doha, Qatar, for us, on the big win.\par \par \uc2 Alex, you have been reporting on this all day, and it is final, 1-0 USA.\par \par \uc2 ALEX HOGAN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Sandra.\par \par \uc2 Well, it's so great to see some of those videos of people celebrating and cheering back home. It's exactly what 