: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I mean, institutions will have no incentives to do anything about the fact that they -- it's like highway robbery how much these degrees cost.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's so wrong. This is so wrong.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: You just brought up the subsidies or the tuition. Look at what happened with the climate bill. They said we're going to give you a subsidy on electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: That same day they raised the price of -- GM and \uc2 Ford\uc2  , of those vehicles by the same amount as the subsidy.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Are you saying tuition prices are going to go up $10,000 tomorrow?\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Why wouldn't they? I mean, when you look at how hard the universities even pushed back against the provisions in the bill that would hold them a little bit more accountable for the huge coffers that they're sitting on. I mean, some private institutions could pay -- make it free for the rest of the time. That's how well Harvard has managed their money, and I know we're not talking about Harvard for this.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So, this goes back to the fact that -- if you look at polls ever since the Biden administration started, do you think this president cares about things that you care about? Those -- his polling on that has been really bad.\par \par \uc2 And then this one when you're looking just like fundamental fairness for people who are out there, basically being told that the Inflation Reduction Act is something great that the gas and groceries are going to go down in price when they realize, actually it was for -- all for climate change.\par \par \uc2 They've -- I think that the exacerbating feelings that there is, the problem as you said, the little guy has to pay for the big guy constantly.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: You're trying to solve the world with first world problem solvers and most of us live on down on the earth and we got to deal with real stuff and that's about that first world stuff.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: So, you have a graduate degree?\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: I do not. I'm with you. And I am the most successful person in my family. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Thank you. Thank you. Alright.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: All your relatives are really offended right now.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: I'm also bigger than they are. I got your back here.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's okay. And they're also not watching. My relatives, not watching. Coming up, Republicans ready to make Dr. Fauci's life another nightmare as the top doc calls it quits.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Republicans vowing to make Dr. Fauci's life very difficult as the nation's top infectious disease expert hangs up his lab coat. Fauci will be stepping down as President Biden's chief medical advisor in December ending nearly a half century in government. Dr. Fauci has been a lightning rod of criticism over his handling of the pandemic and push to lockdown the country.\par \par \uc2 One op-ed says, "Fauci should simply just fade away." "The New York Post" editorial board bidding "Good Riddance to Dangerous Dr. Fauci" calling his COVID guidance disastrous. Fauci making the media rounds to defend himself from the onslaught. Watch here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY FAUCI\uc2  , DIRECTOR, NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF ALLERGY AND INFECTIOUS DISEASE: With COVID, I mean, the things that we thought we knew in the beginning turned out as the months went by to not be the case, that was interpreted by many as flip-flopping or not really knowing what's going on when it really was the evolution of the science.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL MADDOW, MSNBC NEWS HOST: There is a weird obsessive violent ongoing demonization of you by the right that is hinged on COVID.\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: What we're dealing with now is just a distortion of reality making it look like trying to save lives is encroaching on people's freedom.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: But while he might be done with his job, Congress is not done with him. Republicans vowing they will hold Fauci accountable if they win back control in November.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JOHN KENNEDY (R-LA): Dr. Fauci retirement or not is going to be spending a lot of time in front of a congressional committee and committees if Republicans take back control.\par \par \uc2 REP. JAMES COMER (R-KY): He hasn't ever testified in front of the House since COVID started. So, there are so many questions that members have. We've already told Dr. Fauci to preserve all of his documents.\par \par \uc2 RON DESANTIS, GOVERNOR OF FLORIDA: I hope if Republicans take control that they will get to the bottom of everything, from the origins of COVID to all the manifest failures of the public health establishment particularly Dr. \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Alright. Tyrus, so, he'll -- he's going to say goodbye in December. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: He ain't going nowhere. I mean, he's not even going to wear a mask on the masked dancer. I feel like this dude's going to be everywhere. He's going to be working on throwing pitches, doing every possible T.V. show. He's going to give Dr. Drew Pinsky a run for his money. He's going to do his tours and stuff.\par \par \uc2 The only thing I just -- at this point, we need to focus on getting this country back on track. We get -- if the Republicans get the House, start fixing things that matter. Chasing Fauci because he's -- you can't argue with science. It's like arguing with somebody's religion. Apparently, it changes all the time. So, that's going to be his defense. Well, we didn't know this but now we know that and we would have done this. You know, it'd be like that country song, if I knew now what I didn't know then.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: So, and it's going to be a lot of stuff and it's going to get away. It's going to be a huge distraction. He's gone. Let's -- he got -- he was smart. He left because he knew the firing was coming. So, you know, he keeps his pension and we're going to have to deal with him on T.V. shows, but we need to get back to business and shoring up to where the next time something like this happens, we have people in place that don't make those kinds of mistakes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He did a lot of media, a lot.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: That's what I'm saying.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And they accepted almost every invitation. Here is just a montage of some of the media reacting to Dr. Fauci's decision.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Always pushing for science first in President Trump's White House, Fauci at times exasperated, his face in hand.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: The doctor who guided the U.S. through the coronavirus pandemic and saved countless lives --\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: There has never been anyone else like him and there never will be again.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: He was through the face of the messaging as he was pushing strategically and diplomatically against a president who often was pushing in the wrong direction.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I don't think it's an exaggeration to say that there are millions of human beings alive today who would not be alive if not for the work that Dr. Fauci did, coordinated, and led.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Wonder if they would say the same about President Trump and "Operation Warp Speed" but maybe not.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Why aren't the journalists treating this guy like a dangerous quack? We have all the evidence that the lockdowns destroyed small businesses, a generation of children, didn't save lives. I mean he was letting people cross the border in droves unvaxxed, but he was like no don't fly in from Canada. What is this guy doing?\par \par \uc2 He has destroyed this country. You don't do