iot. I mean, he's not that smart. But he's smart enough to know that you can't be a national politician and run on free injection sites. Are you going to have people sitting around like Uma Thurman in Pulp Fiction, they're just going to stab you in the chest plate at the bullseye when you start frothing at the mouth? Absolutely not. Are you going to be on stage during the Democratic primary debate and the moderator is like, who is pro opium den? And you're the only hand goes up? No, no, no, he can't do that. W\par \par \uc2 hat I don't understand is the mentality of these drug people. Yes, you want cutting-edge drug therapy. I'm fine with that. But the goal should be to get people off drugs. The goal should not be to encourage people to do drugs and have them not die, right? Like, you can't have oh, here's Bonnie from the \uc2 Health and Human Services Department\uc2  . She's going to tie this little band around your bicep and you're going to inject black tar heroin into your vein and then she's going to be there in the air conditioning room next to City Hall and give you like a little juice cup afterwards. I mean, we just got cannabis legalized in 19 states. That took two decades. We're not going from that to that.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes, I agree. So, Jessica, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  has made the case that if Democrats choose a white guy, presumably \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  , that Black female voters who are as you know, the most loyal, you know, demographic in the Democrat party, that they will be furious, and they will sit out in the election. True or not?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: So, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  , I hate to say it, does not have his finger on the pulse of the Democratic Party. It's not really his claim to fame. I do think that there's a tremendous constituency certainly led by Black women that will be upset of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  , who is the sitting Vice President, isn't the person who's been nominated and 2024.\par 