ybody.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020220604ei6300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 The Johnny Depp/Amber Saga Drama In The Court Is Over, And The Jury Both Gave Them A Verdict But With Johnny Depp Winning His Case; Republican Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  And Democrat Senator Richard Blumenthal Meets In The Middle Over Gun Issues And Try To Nail A Deal That Would Strengthen Red Flag Laws In The Country; NBC News Reports That President Biden Isn't Pleased With His Aides Always Trying To Walk Back His Words Which Makes Him Look Weak; Biden In Turmoil: President Furious At Staff For Walking Back Gaffes; \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  Cracking Down On Remote Workers; Paywatch: Highest-Paid LA County Lifeguards Earn Up To $500K\b0\par\par\uc2 Greg Gutfeld, Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters,  Shannon Bream \par \uc2 8,874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: So, it could be a busy and active season. Close out taking a look at the corner of wall and broad where we saw the Dow slide. It starts the month all. Hand a bit of on a sour note here but we still got what, 29 days to go. So, anything can and probably will happen. For now, it's about interest rates and inflation. Always.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS HOST: Hi, I'm Greg Gutfeld along with Judge Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters and evil Shannon Bream. THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you find that Mr. Depp has proven all the elements of defamation? Answer, yes. As against Amber Heard, we, the jury, award compensatory damages in the amount of $10 million. As against Amber Heard, we, the jury, award punitive damages in the amount of $5 million. Do you find that Ms. Heard has proven all the elements of defamation? Answer, no.\par \par \uc2 As against John C. Depp II, we, the jury award compensatory damages in the amount of $2 million.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The conclusion of the blockbuster defamation trial between Johnny Depp and Amber Heard did not disappoint. The jury finding that both Hollywood stars defamed one another with Depp emerging as the big vector. Johnny Depp being awarded $15 million bucks after jurors unanimously decided that Amber Heard libeled him with actual malice when she wrote the 2018 \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  op-ed identifying herself as a victim of domestic Abuses.\par \par \uc2 Heard rocking up a win on her counterclaim with the jury deciding she was defamed by Depp's agent who called her abuse allegations a hoax. Heard is being awarded $2 million bucks but is calling the ruling a setback for women.\par \par \uc2 Depp wasn't there to celebrate. He was too busy rocking out in London but he did release a statement, quote, "false very serious and criminal allegations were levied at maybe via the media which triggered an endless barrage of hateful content. Although no charges were ever brought against me, it had already traveled around the world twice within a nanosecond and had a seismic impact on my life and my career. Six years later, the jury gave me my life back. I am truly humbled."\par \par \uc2 Now we are blessed on THE FIVE to have some sound legal minds here, people that have actually gone to law school, one was even a judge so let's go to probably the most legitimate legal mind here. Jesse!\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Were you surprised by this verdict?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: He's actually going to him.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I'm actually going to him. he said come to me last.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS HOST: He did.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: He said, I have nothing to say.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: He said come to me last.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I have followed this trial so closely. Where do we begin?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Well remember what we talked about at the beginning that --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: -- how Depp was willing to risk his reputation as a drunk in order to erase the reputation of being an abuser. So, he was willing to lay everything out there and say I will let you make fun of me for the pills and whatever but I'm not an abuser. And that's what he did.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's kind of like the Russia hoax with Trump.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Right.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You know, they come out and smear you with false allegations and you never get your reputation back.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, you don't.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: So, you have to sue and that's what the president likes to do. Very similar, I haven't followed this as closely as the Sussmann trial. But --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'd be happy to talk about that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You would?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: OK.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We are talking about --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We'll get there in a