o be a lifeguard?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: What -- are they like lifeguarding the La Brea Tar Pits? I don't - - I don't believe this for a second. No, they have to tell me who these people are because that's crazy. Are they on like an oligarchs yacht? Like, a half a million for lifeguards?\par \par \uc2 BREAM: They are on the beaches.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I don't know. This really ticks me off Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, then I'll take it back.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Why don't -- you are on the news side. Bring the facts.\par \par \uc2 BREAK: Listen, you couldn't pay me half a million dollars to run around on my swimsuit. Jesse, I suspect to be a lot less for you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's an abuse of overtime. It happens on the Long Island Railroad. It happens all in these municipalities. They run up the clock on the OT, and you get half your base salary from overtime. We're on to you. We are on to you.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: I mean --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I wouldn't -- I wouldn't let that happen if I ran the show.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Are we having lifeguards at like, midnight when it's dark outside? I don't know how they get the overtime.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, check their time cards when they punch.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: When they punch out with that little wooden booth they sit in. We know what's going on in there, Jessica.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: What is going on?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Impeach Biden.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: So, I'll come full circle from the A to the E block. I don't know how you rack up quite that much overtime but controversial opinion I guess from what we've heard so far on the table. First Responders should be paid more than they are paid. And they serve -- if we're going to start paying cops and firefighters $5,000 a year --\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Yes. I think you'd get a lot of yes votes at this table.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But also, lifeguards do rescue people from drowning. Last time -- what is wrong with you?\par \par \uc2