LD: My parents taught me that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, it was at the gate.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Well, that's -- OK, if it's at the gate then all bets are off. All right, tonight, I got the Evil Shannon Bream on my show, Kash Patel, Kat Timpf, and Tyrus. He's back. Flights keep getting canceled, dammit. Anyway, that's tonight. Good. Let's do this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Animals are great! Animals are great! Animals are great!\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I can't believe you ate it. (INAUDIBLE). Oh, my God. Lord help us all. All right, baby sloth reunited with its mother. Let's take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We saw this last week.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Did we?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, we didn't. That was a different sloth. That was a different sloth, Judge.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Do all sloth look alike? '\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Really?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know what you are? You're a slothist. You are slothist.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: That is so cut.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Look how adorable that is. And it didn't even write a thank you note.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We need more of this.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's adorable. And that's -- I believe that's a marijuana leaf right there.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: No wonder he's so slow.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's at the Jaguar Rescue Center. OK, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I just want to thank whoever sent me the cinnamon and crusted pecans from Alabama to the office. It's delicious. I ate them all weekend.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You didn't offer them to me.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No, I ate them all. That's why. Happy birthday to Emma. She is 30 today. We had a big celebration. Hair was a little out of control.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Happy birthday.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: My hair not hers. Over the weekend, at Burton Betty's we're up on the deck there. Jesse Jr. was very