 distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020220602ei6100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 President Biden Is Blaming Everything Bad Happening Under His Administration To The Ultra MAGA Crowd, And Republicans Are Hitting Him Back By Calling Out His Inaction On Inflation And Rising Commodities That Are Choking American Families; Liberal Media Defends President Biden By Pointing Their Fingers To His Predecessor And To Putin Price Hike; The Media Went Hysterical After \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  Announced That He's Going To Lift The Ban On Former President Trump's \uc2 Twitter\uc2  Account; Experts Say That Rising Crimes In Big Cities Are Making People Skeptical Of Going Back To Their Offices; Liberal City Crime Surge: Growing Violence Threatens Workers' Return To Office; Fentanyl Flooding America: Overdose Deaths Hit Record Number Last Year; No Idea How To Fly: Passenger Takes Over After Pilot Loses Consciousness\b0\par\par\uc2 Neil Cavuto, Jeanine Pirro, Geraldo Rivera, Jesse Watters, Martha  MacCallum, Brian Kilmeade \par \uc2 8,718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Guys, thanks you all very, very much. I want to put that in perspective because having lived through the 70s, the backdrop wasn't -- wasn't like that then. So, with all the problems and all the selling, just a little perspective. Try to enjoy yourself.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS HOST: Hello, everyone. I'm Judge Jeanine Pirro along with Geraldo Rivera, Jesse Watters, Martha MacCallum, and Brian Kilmeade. It's 5 o'clock in New York City, and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 The GOP is heading back hard as President Biden tries to blame the ultra MAGA crowd for his endless economic problems, Scranton Joe rolling up his sleeves to shovel his nonsense talking points on inflation.\par \par \uc2 The president out in farm country today pushing the same, tired talking points. Blaming Putin and those greedy corporations. Biden refusing to take responsibility as we learn the surge in prices is stuck at a 40-year-high. GOP lawmakers calling out the president for his inaction.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOM COTTON (R-AK): \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will blame anyone but himself for this. He's blamed chicken farmers, and the coronavirus, and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and everyone else under the sun.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: President Biden is flailing around, swinging blindly, hoping that something will land.\par \par \uc2 SEN. JOHN KENNEDY (R-LA): The truth is that the Biden administration just keeps kicking its own ass after 14 months, nothing is built. Nothing is back, and nothing is better.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: He was supposed to give his ideas on inflation yesterday. What were his ideas? It's everybody else's fault but his.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: As Biden gets blamed for record inflation, he is finding one group willing to defend his atrocious record on the economy. Guess who?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOY BEHAR, CO-HOST, ABC: A Democrat in office, the deficit goes down, the economy flourishes, and the Republican comes in and destroys it all. And then the next Democrats to come in and it sweep it up.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN, CO-HOST, ABC: We defend the former guy, because I won't. But I will say until the pandemic, the economy was soaring. We had record economic --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Well, because we had President \uc2 Barack Obama\par \par \uc2 WHOOPI GOLDBERG, CO-HOST, ABC: Biden is the guy who said, listen, we need to give people more money. He's in the room with loose boards, he takes a step over here, he gets hit by the war.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GOLDBERG: He takes a step over here, he gets hit by gas going up. And it's not on him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And where is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's task force on this? Parents growing increasingly desperate over a national shortage of baby formula. Forty percent of America's supplies are out of stock.\par \par \uc2 OK, Jesse, I will start with you. Do you think that people who are sitting at their kitchen table trying to pay their bills already paying 5,000 more than they did than last year to maintain the same standard of living give a damn about who is to blame as opposed to what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to do about it?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: I'm just trying to figure out what they said on The View.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN KILMEADE, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: That was crazy.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It was over my head, I think.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Really, really enlightening. Apparently if you listen to The View, if you're sitting around the kitchen table, everything is terrible but none of it is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's fault. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  came in he was supposed to care more and he was supposed to be more confident. And it's clear now he is neither.\par \par \uc2 Right now, he went to a farm, and I know he's not running for reelection, because do you know where the farm was? The farm was in Illinois. If you are running for reelection, you go to a farm in Iowa. This guy is gone, he's not even going anywhere. and he wasn't even in front of like some nice corn stocks or anything like that.\par \par \uc2 You've got to go out -- if you're going to a farm, you got to see a farm. You have to see green, you got to see stocks, I couldn't see any of it. Here is the other thing. He goes out there and he says that the farmers are going to get technical assistance from the government.\par \par \uc2 Do you think farmers need help from the government? The farmers, they don't need help. They know how to plant crops. What's the government going to tell the farmers to do? And by the way, it's a little too late for that help. They plant crops based on seasons. They have systems.\par \par \uc2 We knew when Ukraine was invaded, what, two and half months ago that this was the biggest fertilizer exporter, it's the biggest energy producer, Russia, two and half months later, Joe now says, we're going to do something about fertilizer, food, and energy. Where has this guy been? I don't know where he has been.\par \par \uc2 I know this, all of a sudden, he says big business is like getting in the middle and jacking up prices, because they are greedy. Well, they could have been doing that the last 40 years. Why after 40 years they decide now they are going to get greedy? It doesn't even make any sense.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. Well, you know what, I think that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  thought he was in Iowa when he was in Illinois. But you know what, I will go to you, Martha, because he did. I mean, Jesse is right, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  came in as the empathic sympathetic guy. I mean, that actually got him into office. He cared about COVID.\par \par \uc2 Where is the mercy now that Americans need who can't pay their bills?\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: So, you know, I go back to The View and trying to break down what they were saying there. And I look at what Alyssa Farah said, and the truth is, that the biggest stimulus that we've had to the economy in the last several years was at the beginning of the Trump administration when you had the cutting of regulations and the cutting depreciation, all of those taxes that businesses that are the biggest part of what businesses pay.\par \par \uc2 As soon as that happened, you saw businesses expanding, buying more companies, employing more people, cutting through the red tape and regulation which probably the most effective stimulus to the economy that we've seen in a long time. These are not words that you're hearing cross this president's lips.\par \par \uc2 That is the thing that would generate real growth in this country. When you have inflation and everyone's costs are going up and you got supply chain issues and cost are going up, the best thing that you can do is to cut taxes. Give people relief and give them incentives in order to stimulate their businesses. And that is the most direct way to do it.\par \par \uc2 Whoopi Goldberg says, you know, that he's putting money back in people's pockets. Well, we hear these efforts, we're going to lower prescription drug prices, we're going to make child care cheaper, and that will offset inflation, but that is such a roundabout way to try to get out of it. The most immediate thing you can do is to cut taxes, cut regulation, make it easier for people to open their businesses to make those businesses bigger. We're not hearing any of those really direct things that would actually impact inflation and the economy fairly quickly.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Geraldo, I mean, you've got to have some thoughts on this. I mean, the blame game doesn't work for people who are trying to survive.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Well, I think \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  calling the president incapacitated and incoherent is playing the blame game, Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Do you think he's coherent?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I think that he has in part been very unlucky. There is no doubt that the pandemic and the Ukraine war have had an impact. And there's also no doubt that the president himself with his generosity pouring billions of dollars into the economy has helped fuel the inflation rate. And helped cost come up the supply chain.\par \par \uc2 But now when I hear about him talking about lowering taxes to help people out, that's the last thing I think the economy needs is more money dump in if inflation is this. Now I support a lot of people. You know, I'm blessed that I can. I've never heard them complain more about being on fixed incomes. And it's very, very distressing.\par \par \uc2 The rent went from, you know, $5,000 --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, there's to that.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- whatever it is, I don't know. But it is very distressing and I think that the difficulty is being disciplined enough to find a way out. You've got to cut off the beast. You've got to stop shoveling public money into the trough and expecting, you know, that's not going to burn.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. Well, Brian, I mean, that is the answer. I mean, even the Wall Street Journal is suggesting that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , a.k.a. President Costanza from Seinfeld, do the opposite of what he's done.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Right. We rolled that clip this morning on Seinfeld, I know you don't put the sound when Fox & Friends is on busy working out.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, but I saw your tie this morning. I thought it was beautiful.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: But it's OK. By the way, do you still support Jesse? Is that -- is he still --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I do. But I hope the youngster can really.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Right. You know, everybody has natural -- when you take over you had natural disasters, you have wars, you have challenges, I get it. But when he took over, you can't blame the pandemic. He had a vaccine he's ready to go, he's going to fix things. Then he had 800 billion from Trump and then he chose to spend -- print 1.9 trillion more.\par \par \uc2 And the Ukrainian situation, he told us this was going to happen ahead of time. If he got those weapons quicker this thin could be over already. So, he's made decisions that made everything a lot worse. And I think we've said a lot already but we didn't bring up ultra MAGA. That to me is the problem.\par \par \uc2 Ultra MAGA. He's going to Madison Avenue trying to get a -- trying to get a buzzword to blame somebody. He goes into \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 's 11-point plan and finds one line, on line, on number five, that says I think everybody, the 50 percent that don't pay income tax should pay income taxes, and he wasted all of that time labeling the Trump people and then going to \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 's plan from Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 I was following \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  in Florida. I don't know what I was thinking. Because he was -- he is in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: The archenemies in the wrong state.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: So, by the way, he is not ultra MAGA. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  just a typical conservative Republican.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: He's not \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 . So, he was the wrong -- he had everything messed up. And I resent the fact that he wasted so much time and energy with his staff to try to blame people instead of fixing it. You are 79 years old, stop trying to win the next election, just do your job.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, well, apparently, he doesn't quite know how to fix it, that could be it. Anyway, coming up, the left is flipping out over \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's plan to lift the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  ban on Trump.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Liberals crying fowl after \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  announced he would reverse the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  ban around the world. The permanent suspension of at real \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Musk, the world's richest man as you know and soon to be owner of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  says the original decision to quit him was misplaced and even immoral.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK, CEO, \uc2 TESLA MOTORS\uc2 : It was not correct to ban \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I think that was a mistake. Because it alienated a large part of the country and did not ultimately result in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  not having a voice. I would reverse the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  ban. It is morally wrong and flat-out stupid.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Flat-out stupid. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  founder and the guy who was flat-out stupid and pulled the plug on Trump, \uc2 Jack Dorsey\uc2 , now admitted he was wrong to ban the former president in the first place. Liberals on social media meantime are throwing a fit. One publication tweeting, this hell side could become even worse.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\uc2  is joining the fury dragging \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in the mud for potentially overturning trump's permanent ban.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2 , COMEDIAN: Speaking of baby, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  says that if his deal to buy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  goes there, he will reverse the ban on our infant former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Good, we have the part-time D.J. who makes flamethrowers and cars that fat in charge of morality now. The guy who named his kids Roman numerals will make sure they don't do anything foolish.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I mean, \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\uc2 , I mean, should you run scared from him, Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I'm not scared of Kimmel. He was not that funny last night, not that I watched.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's inconsistent.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You can't, if you are Trump, you can't go back to a party you have been kicked out of. It's not a good look. You have to be invited back, and then you have to wait. If he gets unbanned, you don't come right back. You wait a day, you wait weeks, you wait a couple months.\p