n and content moderation. He never talks about the Wuhan lab, never talked about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  laptop, never talked about the Russia collusion. So, all the big stories of disinformation that we've all experience over the course of the last five years he didn't mention. But it's the Steve Bannons of the world that are the real threat.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, what I find most interesting is the timing of all of this. Now that we have \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  getting closer to taking over \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , former President of the United States comes out and starts talking about the first amendment and the moderation of that -- of that -- of that concept that is so fundamental to who we are, and it makes us the freest country in the world.\par \par \uc2 The First Amendment, the freedom to speak, freedom to practice religion, and the freedom to assemble. I mean, all of that is fundamental to who we are. And this concept that somehow, they can stop us from communicating, and make no mistake, when we communicate by e-mail, we, years ago we would've done it by mail. And now we're doing it by e-mail. And they are looking at our communications, my e-mails, my letters, so to speak to another person saying, you can't say that, you can't say that. We're going to take you off so you can't repeat this.\par \par \uc2 This is the antithesis of the Constitution and what free speech is all about. And he, what Obama is doing is he is cultivating now the concept that we can moderate things, a content moderation and now we can get rid of disinformation which leads us to the place where, if you don't agree with what I think, you will be shut down.\par \par \uc2 And we've been battling this since, you know, since Biden came and even before that, even before the election. When all of a sudden, a newspaper cannot be transmitted or tweeted or our comments about what is in the news. Or 51 intelligence officers lying and saying it's Russian disinformation.\pa