int and then somebody puts out a counter viewpoint and it all shows up on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . That's the way it should be.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: And Sean, you know this, but they've been trying to censor talk radio for a long time since the 90s.\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: For a long time.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: So, this is not new. It's just a different --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: And by the way, if Harold and I were able to censor our opponents when we ran for Congress, the power of that was immense, we wouldn't -- we wouldn't have to spend money to run races because it's only our viewpoints that's out there.\par \par \uc2 But we got to go. All right. Crime, drug abuse, and homelessness spiraling out of control in a big liberal city. Tucker joins us to talk about his new Fox Nation special. That's next.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Hey.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  exposing the horrible consequences of soft in crime policies ruining America's second biggest city. The suicide of Los Angeles is streaming right now on Fox Nation. Here's a preview.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FABIO LANZONI, ACTOR: They never sought district attorney this bad.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Fabio Lanzoni is an actor and a longtime resident of Los Angeles. He moved out after his home was burglarized twice.\par \par \uc2 LANZONI: He was the district attorney of San Francisco and he destroyed San Francisco. And now you're moving to Los Angeles so he can destroy Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 The crime in Los Angeles has become so bad. Every time you turn the TV on.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: There are a lot of questions about home security and how to keep yourself safe.\par \par \uc2 LANZONI: I've been a victim (Ph) of crime. They burglarized my house a couple of times.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What happened to the criminals who burglarized your house? Are they arrested and convicted?\par \par \uc2 LANZ