elf-defense, to vigilante justice. If people can count on the state to protect them, they will protect themselves because people will protect their families. And you're going to start to see extrajudicial killings in Los Angeles, period.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, no question about that vigilante. Vigilante and then the Kyle Rittenhouse effect. That's right.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: All right, Harold.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Tucker, nice to see you. As you -- as you went through this, did you walk away with maybe some ideas that Gascon should be pursuing? I know -- I mean, there are those who want guns off the street. There are those who want more cops on the street, more training for police officers. I agree with you, we have to prosecute crimes and it seems like Gascon is facing some political pressure. But were there other ideas outside of that, that your reporting and your series has as revealed?\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, this isn't really space travel. I mean, these are issues that human beings have dealt with since they left the case or even before. How do you deter the people you live with from hurting you? And you punish them if they do, and the punishment is swift and certain. It's called deterrence. You do it with your kids you do with your dogs. And this is how all living things learn. Like, touch the stove and get burned.\par \par \uc2 And so, we know what to do. Just enforce the laws that the public creates by voting. That's our system. It has been for hundreds of years. He's the one -- I mean, just like restore what we had and things will be fine. That's the answer.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Sean.\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: So, Tucker, we can see the consequences. And we saw that in part of your -- in your segment. But I think the question is, why is this happening? Why is he doing this? I mean, if you don't have rule of law, you have degradation of society. You don't have a country if you don't have rule of law.\par \par \uc2 And this is a \uc2 George Soros\uc