houghts were.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Shellenberger is amazing. What an interesting, smart guy who actually has the most revealing documentary series I've ever seen done on his iPhone and homelessness ever. It explains why we have it. I mean, the problem with California is so many reasonable people just gave up and left. Well, you and me and like millions of others like us who grew up in the state.\par \par \uc2 It's people like Shellenberger who are staying and fighting to improve it to reclaim it that are going to save the state. I'm really rooting for him strongly.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: All right, truckers Great to see you. And thank you for bringing Americans this crucial reporting and allocation of everything that's going on. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Katie Pavlich, thank you, thank you.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Great to see you. Check out the Suicide of Los Angeles streaming now on Fox Nation. "THE FASTEST" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 FORD JR: Welcome back. Time for "THE FASTEST." First up, more fallout after the spectacular downfall of CNN Plus. The network's shutting down a $300 million streaming service less than a month after it launch. The debacle reportedly leaving fired staffers aghast and furious. We've not had an airing here on the show about this.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, we haven't talked about it at all.\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: Greg has not mentioned it.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR: Greg, you have -- you have thoughts about what's happening.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I have no opinion whatsoever on this. This is the first I've heard. What I find interesting is people criticizing us of gloating over this implosion. They're conflating two things. We're not happy if people lose jobs, we are happy that something -- an entity that was trying to destroy us imploded.\par \par \uc2 CNN has advocated for getting us, you know, thrown off cable to have systems. And they had no problem going around trying to cancel anonymous citizens w