\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I can't because they're going to get -- and they're also going to see other things on my phone. All right, let's do this. Greg's What's In The Back Of This Truck News. All right, here's a little quiz. Let's roll the first clip. Right, there you go. OK, everybody, starting with you, what is behind -- what is in the back of that truck? Guess, Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: A shotgun.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Shotgun. Geraldo?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I don't know. Is he smuggling aliens across?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, geez.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Geraldo, that's what I was going to say.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Gilbert, the guy that just showed you his belly.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Get the simulation --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Be clear that Gilbert was not -- you're not referencing --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No. This is -- that was the name of the guy with a belly.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Alligator.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Alligator. Let's roll it shall we?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Oh, bulldog.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, he's cute.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Good dog. I like that new game.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You guys did a lot.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: There's a new country song that just came out. I want everyone to hear it. Check these guys out playing the keyboards.\par \par \uc2 Yes, all right, there you have it. That's Brooksie, Wesley, and Lady. They're part of a Misfit Crew Sanctuary. And it's a sanctuary that saves horses and kill -- and saves them from you kill pens.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: They make glue out of those.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Exactly, Jesse, Exactly where I was headed with that. They're cut.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right, Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, you know, everybody's been talking a lot of crap about teachers lately, so I wanted to give credit to a teacher, third grade teacher Janice Jenkins, who jumped into action when she heard her student coughing.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, this is -- I can't watch it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The boy runs over to her gasping and pointing to his throat. She quickly performs the Heimlich maneuver on him to clear the airway of the water bottle cap he was choking on the New Jersey Charter School teacher told local media, she didn't think, she just acted. She had been trained in CPR and basic first aid years ago, but had recently taken on a refresher. The community is celebrating her heroic actions. She will receive an award and a proclamation.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: She needs one.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Janice Jenkins.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Good for her.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I used to fake like I was choking to get my good-looking teacher to give me mouth to mouth.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You're a sick man.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It worked every time. All right, this is going out to Greg who's into driverless cars.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Look what they do. One got pulled over by police, the guy hit the gas, all right. Well, not the guy, the robot car fled from the officer. He was oh, goodbye.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: No way.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's what happened.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I love it.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME" tonight, Kellyanne Conway, Dan Bongino, Kat Timpf and Psychedelic Toads. We got the toads in the show.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Give Bongino my love.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I will do that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Bye!\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: "SPECIAL REPORT" is up next with Bret.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020220414ei4d00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Disney\uc2  Isn't Backing Down; Neither Will We; \uc2 Disney\uc2  Sacrificing Their Bottom Line For Wokeness; Buttigieg Fearmongers Over FL Parental Rights Bill; Left Supports Superspreader Events If Elites Host; New Revelations In Hunter Biden Scandal; Shady Klain Says WH Won't Influence Hunter Probe; DEA Warns Of Spike In Fentanyl-Related Overdoses; Russian Missile Strike Hits Crowded Railway Station; President Biden Gives Speech At Union Gathering; President Biden's Difficulty In Giving Speeches Examined; Frito-Lay Company Introduces Cracker Jill Product As Opposed To Cracker Jack; Reporter Examines Practice Of Abortion Provider In Washington D.C.\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Jason Chaffetz, Charlie Hurt, Jeff Paul, Raymond  Arroyo \par \uc2 7,571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Let not your heart be troubled, Laura Ingraham, THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is next. Have a great weekend. We'll see you back here on Monday.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE. Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 We begin tonight with \uc2 Disney\uc2 's identity crisis. Now, \uc2 Disney\uc2  is sticking with its plans, it looks like, to ramp up political involvement in the culture wars. Now, if you wondered how and why \uc2 Disney\uc2  went from being a family entertainment company to an activist front group, well.\par \par \uc2 Well, we have more insight for you tonight. These new clips emerge from the Reimagine Tomorrow initiative that they started in September. Now, \uc2 Disney\uc2  claims its newfound woke identity is just good business. It's all about targeting their Gen Z customers.\par \par \uc2 But in this leaked online forum with \uc2 Disney\uc2  employees obtained by journalist Chris Rufo, we learned \uc2 Disney\uc2 's real motivation and it goes even further. Here's Karey Burke, president of Disney's General Entertainment Content.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAREY BURKE, PRESIDENT OF \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  GENERAL ENTERTAINMENT CONTENT: They're targeting a younger, I think more open minded. And now we know, as my son texted me this morning, Gen Z is 30 to 40 percent queer than the other generations, mom. So \uc2 Disney\uc2  better get with it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Is this true? I mean, I don't think so. According to the latest Gallup poll, the numbers have definitely gone up. I'm not sure that math is right. But they're just going with it, and against their own history of staying out of specific contentious political battles.\par \par \uc2 CEO \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2  seems to be stirring in his own humiliation play. Or maybe it looks kind of like a hostage tape, begging for the radical fringe, begging for mercy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOB CHAPEK, CEO, THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 : I know that we've got work to do and that work starts with listening. I understand that we've made mistakes and the pain that those mistakes have caused. And I know that our silence wasn't just about the bill in Florida, but about every time an individual or institution that should have stood up for this community did not.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, remember, it was just a few weeks ago when a small but vocal percentage of activist employees bolstered by a lot of outside groups lashed out when the company took no position on Florida's parental rights bill.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, the bill prohibits teachers of very young children from speaking on sexual and gender identity topics in the classroom. That's a big deal now.\par \par \uc2 Now these activist stage walkouts and pummeled \uc2 Disney\uc2  CEO with complaints. And naturally, this sad vision of a man wilted. It's really painful to watch. And it may be painful for \uc2 Disney\uc2  shareholders too. As maybe they should remind their executives who pays the bills for things like this. It's streaming service, and of course, the very expensive theme park admission fees.\par \par \uc2 And listening to Chapek, it sounds like this is just the first political battle that \uc2 Disney\uc2  is going to be entering as part of its new identity.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHAPEK: I pledge to be a better ally for the LGBTQ plus community. Apologize for not being the ally that you needed me to be, and committed to ensuring that our company lives up to its values.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But he's in luck. He has the support now of \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 's grand niece, Abigail Disney, formerly a thorn in \uc2 Disney\uc2 's side who once railed against CEO \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 's fat compensation package. And also, against the mistreatment of workers, she now seems to be totally on board with the magic wokedom.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  op ed that ran this morning, she claimed that those outraged over what \uc2 Disney\uc2  is doing want to 'erase' an entire class of human beings. What?\par \par \uc2 She took special umbrage against yours truly. Can you imagine that? From my warning to corporate America about the dangers of mucking around in these very controversial political issues.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Disney\uc2  heiress might want to show some real courage, though, why not? And take up a pen against China. They're real human rights abuses, or is keeping the cash flow coming from Disney Shanghai, well, maybe more important to this new moral crusader.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is the journalist who obtained all of those \uc2 Disney\uc2  videos, Chris Rufo, Manhattan Institute Senior Fellow; also joining me is Amala Ekpunobi, PragerU personality, former left-wing activist.\par \par \uc2 All right, Chris. You are - speaking of thorns in the side of these woke corporations, \uc2 Disney\uc2  went on to write that, "The only option for corporate leaders is to stand tall for authenticity, generosity, joy and decency. These things are kryptonite for the right-wing agenda. Fortunately, they are also the heart and soul of the \uc2 Disney\uc2  brand."\par \par \uc2 Well, everyone counts except all of these moderate Americans who just want to go and have fun and not be proselytized to, or not have their kids turned into sexual points of perversion for teacher. Your reaction to this?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUFO, MANHATTAN INSTITUTE SENIOR FELLOW: Yes, I mean, it really is the case that \uc2 Disney\uc2  claims to be standing tall. But you saw the video. CEO \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2 , someone who earns $32.5 million a year as his base salary is just absolutely degrading himself every day, day in and day out.\par \par \uc2 And the reality is, is that the conservatives in this country have dealt a major blow to \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 . In Florida, legislators are looking at taking away their special tax breaks. In Congress and DC, conservatives had said, we're not going to extend the \uc2 Disney\uc2  copyrights for Mickey Mouse and other characters that are set to expire next year. That's a multibillion dollar hit against the company.\par \par \uc2 And conservative parents and families all over this country are in revolt against the mouse, because they don't want their kids to be an experimental ground for the kind of sexual engineering of children that is clearly \uc2 Disney\uc2 's gambit.\par \par \uc2 We've seen it in the clips. We've seen the kind of bizarre personalities that are at the helm, whether it's a biromantic, asexual, a bunch of they, thems, whatever the neo-sexual identities might be, those are the people who are calling the shots. They're projecting their own bizarre psychology onto the CEO who just backs down every day.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Amala, as I said, they're targeting your generation. You're Gen Z, right?\par \par \uc2 AMALA EKPUNOBI, PRAGERU PERSONALITY: Right, I am. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I hate all the name - I hate the names of the generations. It's all stupid, but it's so dumb. But there - they admit, that's the group they are after. My point is, most of the Gen Zers aren't going to pay 300 bucks for whatever it costs for a Park Hopper pass. (inaudible) pay that. Their parents or their grandparents pay it. And they're not going to want to foot these bills. Your reaction to all of this?\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: Oh, exactly. Yes, I completely agree with you. I think what their motive here is, is to get children while they're young and infiltrate their minds with this sort of ideology, because they know that if they get these children at a young age, it will stick as it did with me. When I was a young leftist, that stuck with me into young adulthood. So that is really the goal here.\par \par \uc2 I think what they fail to recognize is the power of parents, and that parents are really awake to the indoctrination that they're trying to push on their children. We're seeing them protest at \uc2 Disney\uc2 . We're seeing them cancel their \uc2 Disney\uc2  Plus subscriptions. And they're sending letters to these executives saying, I will not tolerate you thinking that you are the parent of my child and that you get to dictate what my child learns.\par \par \uc2 And we're seeing the horrific outcomes of children learning this sort of gender theory, not just here on \uc2 Disney\uc2 , but in school and in mainstream media and social media. It's devastating.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Pete - I'm going to get to one more of the videos. But before we do that, \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  revealed his thoughts, guys, on the Florida bill. And he did this this morning. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Your husband, Chasten, he's been a vocal critic of what's going on in my state of Florida when the - with the so-called 'Don't Say Gay' law now, which he says will kill kids. Do you agree?\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, SECRETARY OF TRANSPORTATION: Yes, he's right. And I think every law to be judged for the effect it's going to have on real people. This is going to hurt people.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Chris, it's the opposite. This bill protects children's innocence if it still matters to any of these people.\par \par \uc2 RUFO: Yes, I mean, the logic here is so stunning. It's almost to the point of total absurdity. The idea that if you can't teach kindergarteners, five- year-olds about - that they might be pansexual, or asexual, or biromantic, or all of these other new identities, that somehow it's going to be a leading to killing them.\par \par \uc2 One of the \uc2 Disney\uc2  activist partners actually said that this was all a scheme by Republicans to start kidnapping children. The rhetoric is going to the point of insanity. Conservatives have to just sit strong, not give up, and keep fighting against these baseless and ridiculous smears.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Chris, you've done such a service to parents across this country to reveal what's really going on at \uc2 Disney\uc2 . And Amala, just for the edification of our viewers, here's what one \uc2 Disney\uc2  producer wants to include in the shows she's involved with. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I identify as like a biromantic