 They are not doing right by the American people by putting on events like this.\par \par \uc2 JAKE TAPPER, CNN HOST: Health officials across the country who are just abjectly mortified by what they're seeing from the South Lawn.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He's certainly not afraid of killing you and me and 210,000 other Americans through neglect and manslaughter via policy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But now we get trench and commentary like this from CNN's resident medical analyst \uc2 Leana Wen\uc2 . "The Gridiron dinner was probably a COVID superspreader. But events like this should still go on. This is our new normal."\par \par \uc2 Oh, indeed, the new normal must refer to a Democrat as an office, since these were Wen's previous feelings on the issue.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LEANA WEN, CNN MEDICAL ANALYST: I'm very concerned, because if I were to custom design a superspreader event, this is what it would look like. It would look like a lot of people coming from many parts of the country gathered together, no social distancing, not wearing masks. And in fact, even flaunting this public health guidance.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, this new line of thinking has even infected the White House. After \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  tested positive yesterday, pictures emerged of her kissing President Biden. Surely this was alarming to the White House.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT, FOX NEWS: How can you guys say that President Biden was not a close contact with Speaker Pelosi when there's video of the speaker kissing him?\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Well, Peter, the way that it is defined is by the Center for Disease Control, the CDC, and their definition of it is 15 minutes of contact within a set period of time, and within six feet. It did not meet that bar.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But then this morning in an attempt to perhaps get ahead of some of this bad news, White House Communications Director \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2  was a bit less cavalier in her assessment.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KATE BEDINGFIELD\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR: We take precautions to ensure that the President is protected. But I do think it's important to note that it is possible he will test positive for COVID at some point.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Whatever happens with Biden, let's just - she just says, he may test positive. Rest assured the same media and medical experts who misled the U.S. so egregiously throughout 2020 will be back to offer cover for the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 And don't forget, if you can't watch us live, I want you to set a series record on your DVR. We don't want you to miss us. Remember, it's every week night 10pm.\par \par \uc2 And ahead, new details about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's potential entanglements with his son Hunter and China. Plus, what if there's another reason for Republicans to bring up impeachment articles? We'll explain it in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: President has said, that he never spoke to his son about his overseas business dealings. Is that still the case?\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But is that even plausible? Because according to the Daily Mail search of hunters emails, the term big guy returns 41 hits, the most infamous of those being Hunter's business partner James Gilliar's email , "Suggesting that the President was secretly involved in, set to profit from an alleged Chinese influence operation."\par \par \uc2 But it doesn't end there. The Free Beacon is now reporting that members of the Biden family helped Chinese businessman \uc2 Ye Jianming\uc2 , who has suspected links to the CCP and his family obtains visas to the United States.\par \par \uc2 "At the time, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , his Uncle Jim Biden, and his aunt Sarah Biden, were in business with Ye's energy conglomerate, \uc2 CEFC China Energy\uc2 . At the same day, the Bidens embarked on the visa quest, a CEFC executive authorized a $99,000 line of credit for Jim and Sarah Biden."\par \par \uc2 That's just a coincidence. Joining me now is Jason Chaffetz, Fox News contributor and former House Oversight Committee chair.\par \par \uc2 Jason, good to see you tonight. Now, you recently, I know, spoke to some members about this issue. If you can share it with us, what was your advice for how they should handle this?\par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Even though they're in the minority, they need to immediately issue preservation letters. That's how they expand the net, not just to the government records, but to any contemporaneous notes, any other emails outside of this system, telephone, text messages, all of that.\par \par \uc2 The ask for the preservation should start immediately, because it's the bigger broader family that is involved and engaged in this. Then they - once they get in the majority, they can get after the financial records and all the other supporting documents.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. I want to play what the White House Chief of Staff had to say about this issue. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RON KLAIN, WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF: One reason why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in the White House, is he promised that, unlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his White House wouldn't interfere with Justice Department investigations. And that's what's going on here. It's an independent investigation. I'm not going to comment on it, other than to say that we aren't in any way, shape or form, interfering with or influencing the Justice Department's conduct of it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. We already know, though, from the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , don't we, that Joe did ask Garland, or at least spoke to other people in the White House that ultimately got leaked out, that he wanted Garland to act more like a prosecutor. So that's common knowledge around the White House, and it ended up in the press that entire story about what Biden's wishes were.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yes, he's made it very clear some of the press questions. And let's also remember that it was \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , who helped recommend and push Louis Freeh, the former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director in the Clinton administration to do some work.\par \par \uc2 Not only in Romania, but Louis Freeh openly admits that he went in and talked to the head of counterintelligence for the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2 . And as a thank you, he deposited $100,000 into the bank account of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's trust account for his kids, his grandkids.\par \par \uc2 So don't tell me that they're not surreptitiously going around the bend there, and having those conversations at the highest levels of the Department of Justice. They admit it in the emails.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, more details also, Jason, emerging about something we discussed last night. About the four Secret Service employees that in this separate investigation, obviously, are entangled in this alleged bribery scheme inside the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 Now, we haven't been able to independently confirm everything. But RealClearPolitics today is reporting that "Another secret service special agent involved in the alleged bribery is assigned to the President's detail."\par \par \uc2 So Jason, at first, we thought it was just maybe Jill's detail. Now, it's expanded to the President's detail. This issue of the Secret Service and a lot of great people, obviously in the service, but of corruption, and now perhaps these security breaches keeps coming up.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yes, when I was the chairman of the Oversight Committee, I worked actually very closely with \uc2 Elijah Cummings\uc2 . We did a deep dive. And we had to go through a couple of different secret service directors. They lack oversight, the professionalism and has been questionary.\par \par \uc2 Remember, it's a secret service that was out there advertising on pizza boxes. Hey, come on, join the Secret Service, and taxi cabs and whatnot. But the level of professionalism and training and oversight, this is what happens when you kind of get the lack of oversight that they've had in the past.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Jason, they used to be under Treasury, correct? Weren't they used to - used to be oversight under Treasury. Then they were moved to DHS post 9/11. And everything at DHS is a complete mess. So this - none of this surprised me at all. Look at the border. So - I mean - so this doesn't really shock me. All of it needs to be broken up and to be made more accountable, as you said.\par \par \uc2 Final thought, real quick.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Alejandro Mayorkas is in charge of the border. And he's also in charge of the Secret Service. Hmm. I wonder what's going on there? Maybe it there might be a little management issue. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jason, if to rate one to 10, 10 being the best cabinet ever, one being the worst cabinet ever. How do they rank?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Like, zero - negative two, negative 10. How low can you go? It's about as bad as it could possibly be.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, these are political payoff appointments. Jason, great to see you. Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of illegal immigration, suddenly there are Democrats pretending to care about the border. Now, eight of them have been warning Biden about repealing Title 42. Remember, that's the Trump era policy that allowed for immediate turn backs of illegals at the border because of COVID.\par \par \uc2 Now, this list of Senators includes four, who are up for reelection this fall, wouldn't you know it, in hotly contested races? Now, none of them until recently, none of them were strong advocates for border security or none of them, of course, were against Biden's handling of it.\par \par \uc2 I'm talking about Arizona's Mark Kelly; New Hampshire's \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 ; Georgia's Raphael Warnock; and Nevada's \uc2 Catherine Cortez-Masto\uc2 , all of them disasters on the border.\par \par \uc2 So just don't be fooled by any of this. If they end up getting reelected, they'd be more than happy to continue the destructive policies that Biden has been pushing on this country that allowed 2 million illegals to pour across our southern border since he took office, which leads me to what I have been saying for months.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Biden and his DHS Secretary should be impeached for the crime of conspiring to keep the southern border open during a national health emergency.\par \par \uc2 The House could actually bring up a serious perhaps impeachment inquiry just on this issue of the border alone. They impeached a president for Russia collusion.\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And why isn't this border collusion at some point?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When the President conspires to subvert the sovereignty of his own country, how could that not be grounds for impeachment?\par \par \uc2 Now, as you can see, that's what I've contended for some time now. So I was so pleased to see the argument built out by Charlie Hurt in the Washington Times, writing "He has aided and comforted our foreign enemies by publicly inviting illegals to swarm into the country. He has purposefully undermined the Constitution he swore to uphold and defend. It's just that simple."\par \par \uc2 Charlie Hurt, Washington Times opinion editor and Fox News contributor joins me now. Charlie, now you go on to say that President Biden isn't finished and that only strengthens the argument to start threatening this now. Explain that?\par \par \uc2 CHA