ustrated that they can't get booze. Obviously, I have never behaved like that no matter how much I drank. So I don't think it's the entire problem.\par \par \uc2 And you see first class gets all the alcohol, and then coach can't buy any alcohol. So it's also classist. And it's an injustice, I would say. And I think injustice can make anybody angry.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Right.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Gunz, I loved the statement from the company vice president -- quote -- "Customers have expressed a desire for more beverage options."\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Especially when you're stuck on a flight 20,000 feet in the air at least.\par \par \uc2 Yes, I do feel bad for the flight attendants, because they have to deal with all sorts of lunatics to begin with. But, hopefully, people drink enough that they just end up going to sleep. There's the solution.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: The union that represents Southwest said the move is -- quote -- "unsafe and irresponsible." So they clearly do not like that decision.\par \par \uc2 We will see how it goes, because it's going to come back.\par \par \uc2 Thanks to both of you. And have a wonderful weekend.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: You too.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Thanks.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: All right, that will do it for us. I cannot believe it. It is the end of the week and almost the end of Friday.\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for joining us. I will see you back next week.\par \par \uc2 Remember to tune in to "Cavuto Live" tomorrow morning 10:00 a.m. Eastern time. And you can catch me and \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  weekdays 1:00 p.m. Eastern time for "America Reports."\par \par \uc2 Thanks so much for joining us here on "Your World." I'm Sandra Smith.\par \par \uc2 And "The Five" starts right now.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED.