ge, criticized the movie. But the dwarf acting community is not on board with this. Several dwarf actors could now lose their jobs because of this virtue signaling. We've got details on it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So "Game of Thrones" actor, Peter Dinklage went on a podcast the other day and declared that it was quote, "offensive and backward" that \uc2 Disney\uc2  was planning to hire real life dwarves, little people for a remake of the film "Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs." Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETER DINKLAGE, ACTOR: I was little taken back by the very, very -- they're very proud to cast a Latino actress as Snow White.\par \par \uc2 HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: But you're still telling the story of Snow White.\par \par \uc2 HOST: Still Snow White. Yes.\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: And the Seven Dwarfs.\par \par \uc2 HOST: Sure.\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: Take a step back and look at what you're doing there.\par \par \uc2 HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: You know, it makes no sense to me.\par \par \uc2 HOST: But so --\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: Because you're progressive in one way, and then, but you're still making that [bleep] backward ...\par \par \uc2 HOST: Oh.\par \par \uc2 DINKLAGE: ... story of the seven dwarfs living in a cave thinking what the [bleep] are you doing, man?\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So in response to that podcast, podcasts have real power now, the \uc2 Disney Company\uc2  said it was quote, "rethinking" its use of dwarves in the "Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs" remake.\par \par \uc2 Now, some dwarf actors are asking, who put Peter Dinklage in charge of the dwarf community?\par \par \uc2 Dylan Postl played Hornswoggle, the leprechaun in the WWE for 10 years. He also act in "The Muppets." He joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Thanks so much for joining us. So, I think a lot of people hear this podcast and they think well, you know, here's a guy who's got 