ose were shot. And you look at that, and then you read the next stat and it says that is the highest number of police officers killed since the attacks of 911. It is stunning.\par \par \uc2 PETE HEGSETH, FOX NEWS HOST: It is stunning. And it is not hyperbole. We have to be careful sometimes with hyperbole, especially in the cable news business. It is not hyperbole to say it is open season right now on America's police officers. And if you didn't, if you watch this ceremony today, you did not have a dry eye.\par \par \uc2 And you had a much deeper recognition of the reason why these men and women serve in this case, this man and that the wives that served with them. And these people had been dehumanized during a defund movement that has demoralized the police yet elevated the criminal who dehumanize that police officer and feel like the streets are theirs, and there are no consequences because of radical D.A. and the widow pointed that out directly today and got a huge, huge standing ovation.\par \par \uc2 Policies have matter, and the police is bearing the brunt. And if, if a day like today doesn't make you understand that, then you're just on the wrong side of the ledger on this, then you're pro criminal.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: And I want to play that soundbite that Pete just alluded to Joe and then I'll get your response on the other side. This is Jason Rivera's widow talking about, Alvin Bragg. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LUZURIAGA: The system continues to fail us. We are not safe anymore, not even the members of the service. I know you were tired of these laws, especially the ones from the new D.A. I hope he's watching you speak through me right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, she was heartbreaking and compelling, Joe Concha. I mean, you look at what's happening around the country, and what do you think of when you see a widow speak like that?\par \par \uc2 JOE CONCHA, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: I think of