gainst them. How degrading is that?\par \par \uc2 But I don't think crooked could clear the field. Do you? I don't think that Mayor Pete, or Bernie, or Stacey Abrams is scared of Hillary. The machine - - Clinton machine is rusty. There's no Clinton mystique. And I think the Squad would absolutely tear her face right off.\par \par \uc2 But there is a lot of bad blood between Biden and Hillary. Remember when Hillary was Secretary of State, she disrespected \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . She had a lot more influence over \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  than Joe did. Then when Obama was done, he basically anointed Hillary, told Joe to step aside, it was her turn. And then, Joe ended up beating the guy she lost to. And to see Hillary kind of circling you like a vulture must make Joe's blood boil.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I think though that Dana is right on this one. I think that don't count Hillary out. Stay right there. A huge, huge, really huge -- how huge? Very huge announcement about THE FIVE is coming up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Some very big news today about THE FIVE, your favorite show. Judge Jeanine Pirro is going to be a full-time co-host on the show. And Geraldo Rivera, Harold Ford Jr., and Jessica Tarlov will be our permanent rotating co-hosts. The changes officially kick in starting January 24.\par \par \uc2 Harold and Jessica along with -- is that baby Cleo? Yes, I see her.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I want to see the baby.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Holt up. Put the screen up. I want to see her in the camera..\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I want to see her on the screen.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, Cleo.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, she's big.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: She's so cute.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: She's big. We're big. She's big. Everyone is big.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Have you been sleeping.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Congratulations to all of you. Let me start with Harold, what have you gotten yourself into?\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: I hope a good thing. I've been watching the show tonight and taking notes on with Geraldo's performance. And hope we now can collaborate a little bit more, because those guys are tough.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: They are. Tough crowd.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Geraldo, you've, you've watched this show from the beginning. Are you excited to become officially a part of it?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: First of all, huge fan of Jessica and Harold. And of course, you all have been so kind to me, you know, despite the fact that we obviously disagree on some issues. But we agree -- we agree that, you know, we respect each other. We have great affection. And I think it comes across and that's why the show's so successful. And I'm proud to be on it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jessica, well, first, it's great to see you with his lovely baby.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Are you ready to get back in the arena here and have some arguments with Jesse?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I was listening to the show as well. I could -- I'm going to use my last eight weeks for sure before coming back into the arena. And I was thrilled to see that Jesse's New Year's resolution was to be nicer to me. I have a child. I deserve that.\par \par \uc2 But I'm really thrilled to be joining the show. It's obviously a show I watch for years. And I've been thrilled to be colleagues with all of you and newer with Harold, who joined just last year. But it's great to be part of the show that really shows off that people on both sides of the aisle can get along and have fun. And yes, I'm just overwhelmed by this and this.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, good. And Judge Jeanine, let's give you a chance to say a few words to the audience here that adores you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, first of all, I'm thrilled to be a part of this. I mean, I love all of you. And it is for me an opportunity to do a lot of things five days a week. I mean, I've been on the weekends for 11 years now, everybody, with "JUSTICE WITH JUDGE JEANINE." And it's nice to be a part of a team that discusses every big issue every day five days a week.\par \par \uc2 So, I'm thrilled to be part of this and I have great respect for everyone here and affection as well. So, for me it's a wonderful thing.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Awesome.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: My three dogs though, they're very upset about it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: They're worried.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, they are.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: They'll be well taken care of there. Greg, you have anything you want to say here to these folks?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I'm just -- I'm a little bit worried about their choice of music. So, like, I will just have fewer punk rock, fewer metal songs, and it'll just be more country music.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I love country music.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I noticed that Judge Jeanine chose Toby Keith I think today.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And Jesse, I'll give you the last word here.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I'm just going to -- I'm so excited. I want to get back to the table.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Because the best part about this crew here is the conversations in the commercial break. Geraldo's new Bentley or you know talking golf with Hereford Jr. or, you know, my giving Jessica nursing tips and talking to the judge about New York City and our dogs. I can't wait to get back to the table.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, well, it's thrilling. It's a wonderful, amazing show. I know that the three of us are honored to be on it. And now we have all of you with us as well. And thank you to all the fill-ins as well. Everybody, we love you. All right, Judge, Geraldo, Harold, and Jessica, congratulations one more time. "ONE MORE THING" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING." Dana.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, well, it's time for this. Dana's sorry, we're ruining your name news. So, the other day that Washington Post published this