O: Do you feel that way?\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Well, I would say Jimmy giving himself a 5.9 is very generous in this poll. I'm very happy that they asked Jimmy about this. And he said that he is a 5.9 out of 10.\par \par \uc2 So, congratulations, Jimmy, on that.\par \par \uc2 Before we came on, Neil, somebody literally...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: But a 10 on personality, a 10 on personality, which I always argue...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: A 10 on personality.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: ... counted for a lot, yes.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Yes. Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 Somebody tweeted us before we came on saying that Jimmy looks homeless. So that's what we have got going for us.\par \par \uc2 But, in all honesty...\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Stop. Listen, if Gunz...\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: In all honesty, Neil, it is about being -- just being confident with yourself and just being happy about one's abilities, because, listen, you might not be great on looks, but you got the personality, and then you can always crush it.\par \par \uc2 It's the year 2022. We're taking our lives back.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I heard that in high school all the time. Yes, Neil, you're such a nice guy that has a nice personality.\par \par \uc2 No, no. You still have no dates.\par \par \uc2 So, let me switch gears, guys, because this might be explaining the problem here for these guys rating themselves 5.9. They would jump that in order for like this. \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  is offering a new subscription service. I think you pay 10 bucks a month, you get a taco every day. It more than pays for itself, I think after four or five tacos.\par \par \uc2 And there's reports that up-front demand is going to be strong. What do you think, Jimmy?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: The last thing we need under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is more people making a run for the border.\par \par \uc2 And I just think, if we're being honest, this is a dead end to me.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: You're not being...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: But I think -- no, it's a dead end. It's a dead end to me.\par \par \uc2 But I think it'll work with their clientele, because most of their clientele already has a marijuana subscription service, so why not a \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  subscription to boot?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: There you go.\par \par \uc2 Jimmy, I just went to check, is \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  an advertiser? Can we just check that? All right.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Stop being silly.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: I love \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Gun, what do you make of this? Now, Gunz, you would definitely take them up on this.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: Oh, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 In one of my group chats, we have already discussed the subscription service, Neil. But it's all over the place. So I have gone to the Taco Bell Cantina, which actually sells alcohol. I have gone with my friends. We have had \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  parties out there.\par \par \uc2 My niece -- I have a 6-year-old niece. My brother in law talked to me about the subscription service. My niece wants a \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  party, rather than a pizza party, for her upcoming birthday. So all about the \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Wow.\par \par \uc2 GUNZELMAN: I have hung out with friends there. I have got one right now. Let's go, \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  all day long.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I think this is going to be the future.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Wow.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Guys, I really do. I think this is going to be the future of fast food. It's easy money for the big fast food giants.\par \par \uc2 They have the dedicated crowd. I think this is going to be a trend. Does that worry you, Jimmy?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: No.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: No.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: No, it doesn't.\par \par \uc2 Listen, it doesn't worry me, because I do think this is the future. And what I mean by this is the phone, OK, has eaten people long befor