pectful and I'm 66 years old. What am I going to do?\par \par \uc2 He says, well, I'll try talking to him. I mean, sure enough, he comes out on the deck and Alejandro calls up to him and starts conversation with him, you know, a respectful conversation and this young man went off the rails.\par \par \uc2 I told your mother she wasn't going to be living here anymore. I told her not to disrespect me. He just exploded at Alejandro. He told Alejandro, stay right there that this was going to be taken care of that day. Stay right there. I'll be right down.\par \par \uc2 Alejandro is no fool. He grew up on the main streets. He knew what he was dealing with. He knew he was dealing with a gang member and that that gang member was calling for backup.\par \par \uc2 So Alejandro did as far as I'm concerned what he should have done. He started packing his kids in his car and told his mom to hurry up and pack her dog up so they could -- they were leaving for New York City to visit Alejandro's grandmother, visit the great grandma's house.\par \par \uc2 He grabbed the nine millimeter his mother kept on the bookshelf next to the door for her own self-protection because he knew while he was loading things up, things could go sideways and he is a protector. And he's got his kids, he has got his fiancee and he's got his 66-year-old mother.\par \par \uc2 Sure enough, he is putting his kids in the car when the gang member from upstairs comes downstairs with a giant wooden chair crushes it into the sidewalk, picks up one of the heavy wooden legs, and I'm telling you the front yard is probably 20 feet square and it's down a hill. So three or four steps and this guy is on top of him and he coming out and with the club raised.\par \par \uc2 Alejandro shot him three times, cleared the chamber dropped the gun, got in his car got his kids to safety. They didn't want the additional gang members coming back and you know, then there's a real shoot up in who knows what happens.\par \par \uc2 He ended up driving back to Georgia getting his kids safe, getting his fiancee safe, checking himself into the Veterans Administration Hospital because obviously this was a difficult situation and he called and turned himself in.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: And they put him in jail on first degree murder charges.\par \par \uc2 STARK: Where he sits today.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Mike Stark, I hope that you will come back because this is one of those stories that you know, I want to keep tracking because I think it's - - I think it's really important. He sounds like an amazing man. Thank you, Mike Stark.\par \par \uc2 STARK: Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Carlson.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: We are at a time. "The Trial of Kyle" is out today on FOX Nation. I hope you watch it. We will see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020211217ehcg00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 President Biden's Latest Approval Rating Is In Another Low But He Told Late Night Show Host Jimmy Fallon That He Doesn't Follow Polling Anymore; Outgoing Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  Says That Crime Is Down Since He Took Office And It's Been Consistently Down In His Eight Years In Service Despite Reports Of Left And Right Crime In The City; The White House Suggests That It's OK For Kids To Have Their Snacks Or Lunch Outside Even Under Cold Temperatures In Order To Keep Them Safe From The Virus; Dems Push New COVID Restrictions; Kamala Complains: VP Gripes About Ridiculous Negative Media Coverage; Schools Add Ex