l animals including an elephant seal. Check out this sucker. Look at that look. Oh, he's got -- it's coming. It feels so good. It feels so good. I could watch that for days and maybe I will look. Look. It's like me with my allergies. OK.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You know, that feeling is not as good now because of COVID, you know.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And that like it used to be a real pure feeling.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And now it's tarnished with COVID.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Emma's story about sneezing and COVID is the best one ever.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes. (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, I want to tell you about this. The \uc2 University of Houston\uc2 's men's basketball team lost a game to Alabama over the weekend. They were not happy. In fact, they were so mad that the players and coaches actually threw a temper tantrum in response knocking over garbage cans and kicking chairs.\par \par \uc2 But one sophomore on the team, a guard Jamal Shead didn't join in the trash in the arena and walked in the locker room. Instead, he began cleaning up his teammates' mess and has since gotten a lot of attention for his maturity and being such a good role model.\par \par \uc2 The Houston's men's basketball coach apologize for the team's behavior. But Jamal you are good citizen number one.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Oh, they're going to hate Jamal in the locker room.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes. He made the team look bad.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, he made the team look bad. Harold.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR: He's a good kid. We ought to keep reading that story over and over again. Take a look at this. Speaking of good guys.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's white.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes. I'm going to get my phone on.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I got a body camera going. Let's look for it under there.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\