o go out and kill somebody? Guaranteed. It's guaranteed to happen. It does not invalidate the overall approach."\par \par \uc2 Well, senior correspondent Mike Tobin joins us from Waukesha, Wisconsin, with the latest on this. Hi, Mike.\par \par \uc2 MIKE TOBIN, FOX NEWS SENIOR CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Jillian. The bail was set high with the intent that Darrell Brooks, with a record that stretches through his entire adult life, doesn't get out of jail again. Brooks appeared in court wearing one of those suicide prevention suits. He was also wearing a COVID mask. He didn't say anything as he sat at the defense table and the initial five charges of intentional homicide became official.\par \par \uc2 A six charge of homicide is expected as eight-year-old Jackson Sparks died yesterday. More than 500 people or five dozen people, I should say, were also injured. One thing stressed in the hearing is that this attack was no accident.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KEVIN COSTELLO, WAUKESHA COUNTY CIRCUIT COURT: To detectives, not lay people, detectives not only tried to stop this, but rendered an opinion that this was an intentional act. And I've not seen anything like this my very long career.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 Tobin: Court document show that when the red Ford SUV driven by Brooks came through the barricades, it was going slow enough that the police detective, Casey, was able to pound on the hood, get a look at Brooks and tell him to stop. The vehicle sped up as he got into the crowd of people. Doorbell video shows Brooks arriving at the home of Daniel Ryder 20 minutes after the attack. He was cold and said he was waiting for an Uber.\par \par \uc2 Ryder didn't know about the attack and fixed him a sandwich. Ultimately, police arrived and arrested Brooks. More information about the November 2nd attack, which Brooks is accused of punching the mother of his child in the face and running her over with an SUV, we know now that she was injured 