-PORTER: Say that to my wife.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, I bet. Well, thank you for doing it because we need it. Carl Tharp-Porter. Good to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 THARP-PORTER: All right now. Take care.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So Mike Rowe has spent a lot of his life with truck drivers and people who make the country work. He spent a lot of his life highlighting the importance of blue collar jobs and the strong work ethic.\par \par \uc2 The media is mad at Mike Rowe for that. He is not political by the way. They say it's conservative to be in favor of work. We'll ask him about that, next.\par \par \uc2 We're seeing a live look at where the Patriot Awards -- FOX Nation Patriot Awards are going to be tomorrow. You can watch all your favorite FOX hosts. We hope we are you're favorites. Anyway go to foxnation.com/patriot awards for tickets. It's tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Mike Rowe is a well-educated white collar kind of guy. He spent most of his life however with blue-collar people, the ones who actually keep the country running and unlike most people in the media, he treats them with respect. He is only interested in what they do he thinks is meaningful.\par \par \uc2 Well, he is hated for that. "The Republic" just published a piece accusing Rowe of quote, "sneaky conservatism," it is hard to even say the words.\par \par \uc2 Mike Rowe is the host of "How America Works" on FOX Business, the founder of "Mike Rowe Works Foundation" and he is also the host, of course of "Dirty Jobs," that show is coming back to Discovery on Sunday, January 2nd. They never should've taken it off. They know that now.\par \par \uc2 Mike Rowe joins us to respond to this piece. Mike Rowe, good to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 MIKE ROWE, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK HOST, "HOW AMERICA WORKS": You sneaky show host.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, so we are opposites that way. I just say exactly what I think. You don't seem very political to me. Why did they 