hen you go to real-world data like Australia where they implemented an outdoor mask mandate on July 15 and cases went up 600 percent. They go, no, not that data, it's the data the CDC said it's in causal. That's the data on mask that matter. It's not what the story said.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I did say natural immunity, though.\par \par \uc2 SCAVINO: No, you did. You did.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: You did. It's a good thing. Joey, you know, you're from Georgia. Right?\par \par \uc2 JONES: And I don't get to say the name of that movie on TV because when I talk about it --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: It could sound a little different.\par \par \uc2 SCAVINO: That's why I said O. There is an O.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: But Joey, I mean, the rest of the country really has been back to normal for almost a year now. We've gone from 15 days to slow the spread to turn in your employment. Right?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JONES: We've been back to normal since March 16, 2020 then where I live.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 JONES: But when you say that the mandates are working, they are working and getting people to do something that they are morally conflicted about, they are working and making them do it anyway. Listen. I'm vaccinated. I don't mind to tell people that. I chose to do it when I was in the marine corps. I don't know what vaccines I got. I'd be a hypocrite --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: There are 17 of them.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes. I'd be a hypocrite to question one now, you know? But with all that being said, I would trust an unvaccinated healthcare worker that saved my life and took care of me for a year over a vaccinated and boosted bureaucrat that's only doing this because the politics work out for them in their mind.\par \par \uc2 That's where I struggle with this. I can tell you about a gold star wife who is struggling to keep her job and using every exception she can found. It's not my right or job to tell her if s