ead as much or more than children. So, it's vitally important if you're going to make the kids wear a mask. I think you have to have the teachers get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: This is one of those rare cases where the president the teachers union agrees with you Admiral. So we'll see what happens on that front. Thank you, sir, for taking the time.\par \par \uc2 GIROIR: You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: By the way if you are not being rushed back to in person work, and let's say you really like doing it the old virtual way. \uc2 Google\uc2  has some news for you. You're welcome to keep that going. But we're going to catch your pay. After this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: \uc2 Google\uc2  and voice, so you can keep doing the virtual thing, but we just might cut your pay as a result of the 15% depending on where they live.\par \par \uc2 Charlie Gasparino has been crunching those numbers. Charlie could easily afford a 15% pay cut is that a principle. But what do you make of this? I mean, I bet you --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GASPARINO, FBN SENIOR CORRESPONDENT: please.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GASPARINO: It'll be a trend. You know, you can already hear it coming out of Wall Street. You know, James Gorman, the CEO of Morgan Stanley, who famously recently said that, you know, if you want to live in, if you make New York salaries, you shouldn't be living in Denver. So, you know, you can see people are starting to calculate, like, if my workforce wants to work out of town or stay at home, you know, it's going to reflect, their pay is going to reflect that just another way. Businesses can cut, cut expenses.\par \par \uc2 But I will tell you this, in certain jobs, they may not have the ability to do that. I mean, there -- I mean, listen, if you're a very good investment banker, or a very good broker, you know, James Gorman cuts your pay cut, you're going to go to \uc2 UBS\uc2 , which has no way they 